@namespace PoPunkouterSoftware.Client
@page "/settings"
@rendermode WasmRenderModes.Interactive

<PageTitle>Settings · PoPunkouterSoftware</PageTitle>

@* Nothing to set (owner's call, 2026-11-17). The four preferences this page used to hold —
   Theme, Density, Sound, Details — are fixed for everyone: the theme follows the device, the
   layout is compact, there is no sound, and every detail shows (see js/theme-kit.js, which
   also deletes the old stored choices). The route and the header gear stay: the estate
   standard puts a settings control at the upper right, and this page is where it leads,
   saying plainly what the app does instead of offering switches. *@
<main id="main-content" class="app-page settings-page" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
        <h1>Settings</h1>
        <p class="app-note">There is nothing to change here — the app is set up the same way for everyone.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="app-card settings-fixed" aria-labelledby="settings-fixed-title">
        <h2 id="settings-fixed-title" class="app-card-title">How the app looks and behaves</h2>
        <dl>
            <dt>Theme</dt><dd>Follows your device's light or dark setting.</dd>
            <dt>Layout</dt><dd>Compact, so more fits on a small screen.</dd>
            <dt>Sound</dt><dd>None.</dd>
            <dt>Details</dt><dd>Everything shown — build, page, package and error chips, performance trends, and repo links in Ctrl+K.</dd>
            <dt>Build</dt><dd>v@(BuildStamp.Value)</dd>
            <dt>Sign-in</dt><dd>None. The app has no accounts.</dd>
        </dl>
    </section>
</main>
